    "schema_diff_summary": "syntax_cache.rs has one test module named tests. Add the new test function at the end of that module, before its closing brace. Do not write a second mod tests. Change only count_newlines. A lone LF counts as one. A lone CR counts as one. A CR LF pair counts as one. Do not count U+2028, VT, FF, or NEL. Do not write one arm for LF and another arm with the same count for CR. Do not write two if arms that return the same value. Combine them with ||. That is clippy::if_same_then_else. Do not touch region_of, regions_of, or line_text. The existing test rehighlight_stops_when_state_converges stays green. Do not rewrite its assertions. The test a_carriage_return_counts_as_one_line checks count_newlines of a, CR, b is 1. a, CR, LF, b is 1. a, LF, b is 1. a, CR, CR, b is 2. Branch from the current tip of main. base_sha records that tip at planning time. If main has moved, use the new tip. Keep the change under about 60 lines. Stay inside this one behavior. Do not add VT, FF, NEL, or U+2028. Run the full test module named in the commands, not only the new test."
